WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:48.152 --> 00:50.613
‎CUBA, 2014

4
00:53.533 --> 00:55.243
‎She's not answering.

5
00:56.244 --> 00:58.162
‎Do you think something happened?

6
00:58.246 --> 01:00.165
‎Of course not.

7
01:01.916 --> 01:03.626
‎Jeez, that girl…

8
01:04.711 --> 01:05.962
‎Damn it.

9
01:07.130 --> 01:09.048
‎Let's wait a bit longer.

10
01:09.549 --> 01:10.425
‎Hui-suk.

11
01:11.718 --> 01:13.636
‎I can't believe this punk.

12
01:13.720 --> 01:15.597
‎How could she miss her own graduation?

13
01:16.347 --> 01:18.641
‎We've waited so long for this day…

14
01:28.276 --> 01:30.278
‎We've waited for so long.

15
01:32.280 --> 01:34.616
‎Just wait until she gets home.

16
01:35.450 --> 01:37.160
‎I'll teach her a lesson!

17
01:41.122 --> 01:42.582
‎-My word. ‎-Goodness.

18
01:44.167 --> 01:46.586
‎-Well, I'll just… ‎-Wait, Hui-suk.

19
01:46.669 --> 01:47.587
‎Hey, Su-jeong.

20
01:48.254 --> 01:49.088
‎Su-jeong.

21
01:51.090 --> 01:53.760
‎My word, how much did you eat?

22
01:53.843 --> 01:54.802
‎Goodness.

23
02:00.934 --> 02:03.937
‎I was planning to go ‎after observing the surgery a bit.

24
02:04.687 --> 02:05.563
‎I'm sorry.

25
02:05.647 --> 02:07.941
‎If you only observed, ‎why is there blood on your face?

26
02:09.108 --> 02:11.986
‎Since I skipped graduation ‎to observe the surgery,

27
02:12.070 --> 02:14.697
‎they said I might as well give it a shot

28
02:14.781 --> 02:15.990
‎and told me to get closer.

29
02:16.074 --> 02:17.075
‎So then I…

30
02:18.451 --> 02:19.661
‎I'm sorry.

31
02:19.744 --> 02:21.788
‎Here you go.

32
02:24.666 --> 02:25.500
‎Wow!

33
02:26.042 --> 02:28.419
‎My gosh, Eung-gu. ‎Where'd you get something so rare?

34
02:29.045 --> 02:32.465
‎Your aunt made it herself ‎to congratulate you.

35
02:33.049 --> 02:36.469
‎Do you know how hard it is ‎to find white rice in Cuba?

36
02:42.058 --> 02:42.976
‎Su-jeong.

37
02:43.059 --> 02:44.435
‎Look at us.

38
02:45.103 --> 02:47.313
‎We got dressed to the nines

39
02:47.397 --> 02:49.190
‎since it's a once-in-a-lifetime event.

40
02:51.276 --> 02:52.735
‎Did you just laugh?

41
02:53.236 --> 02:54.988
‎You could've put this cap on,

42
02:55.071 --> 02:56.406
‎then let your aunt try it on.

43
02:56.489 --> 02:58.116
‎I could've tried it on too.

44
02:58.199 --> 02:59.701
‎Then we could've taken photos,

45
02:59.784 --> 03:01.911
‎just like everyone else for a change.

46
03:08.376 --> 03:09.627
‎I'm sorry.

47
03:12.422 --> 03:13.256
‎Darn it.

48
03:16.134 --> 03:17.635
‎But then again,

49
03:17.719 --> 03:19.137
‎who raised her, huh?

50
03:19.721 --> 03:21.347
‎You did, Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

51
03:21.431 --> 03:22.724
‎It's your fault, really.

52
03:32.191 --> 03:33.484
‎Time to make a wish.

53
03:44.454 --> 03:49.542
‎"As a member of the medical profession…"

54
03:50.126 --> 03:54.630
‎As a member of the medical profession…

55
03:55.340 --> 03:59.927
‎"I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life ‎to the service of humanity."

56
04:00.720 --> 04:04.807
‎I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life ‎to the service of humanity.

57
04:05.933 --> 04:10.688
‎"I will practice my profession ‎with conscience and dignity."

58
04:12.065 --> 04:16.527
‎I will give my teachers the respect ‎and gratitude which is their due.

59
04:18.821 --> 04:24.494
‎"The health and well-being of my patient ‎will be my first consideration."

60
04:24.577 --> 04:29.999
‎The health and well-being of my patient ‎will be my first consideration.

61
04:32.085 --> 04:37.131
‎"I make these promises as a medical doctor

62
04:37.840 --> 04:41.427
‎solemnly, freely, and upon my honor."

63
04:45.348 --> 04:50.186
‎I make these promises as a medical doctor

64
04:50.269 --> 04:54.899
‎solemnly, freely, and upon my honor.

65
05:14.043 --> 05:16.587
‎Presenting Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

66
05:17.255 --> 05:18.089
‎Yeah!

67
05:21.843 --> 05:23.177
‎Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

68
05:24.137 --> 05:25.263
‎You made me a doctor.

69
05:26.806 --> 05:27.974
‎Thank you, Aunt.

70
05:35.898 --> 05:37.692
‎Let's take a photo.

71
05:41.279 --> 05:42.113
‎All right.

72
05:52.832 --> 05:55.710
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

73
06:07.305 --> 06:08.222
‎Now, Kocher maneuver.

74
06:08.306 --> 06:11.184
‎KOCHER MANEUVER: DISSECTING THE DUODENUM ‎&amp; PANCREATIC HEAD FROM SURROUNDING TISSUE

75
06:12.351 --> 06:14.353
‎I told Ms. Go, just in case.

76
06:14.437 --> 06:15.438
‎She'll be here later.

77
06:20.943 --> 06:24.280
‎I can't help but wonder ‎who Gye Su-jeong really is.

78
06:25.281 --> 06:26.616
‎Is Gye Su-jeong…

79
06:29.118 --> 06:31.787
‎Doctor X?

80
06:42.089 --> 06:43.007
‎That's right.

81
06:44.675 --> 06:47.678
‎She's Doctor X.

82
06:50.389 --> 06:51.349
‎Then…

83
06:53.643 --> 06:55.811
‎Then the surgery results--

84
06:55.895 --> 06:59.941
‎If Doctor X puts a patient's life ‎and well-being above all else,

85
07:00.691 --> 07:01.567
‎then yes.

86
07:02.568 --> 07:04.737
‎Gye Su-jeong is Doctor X.

87
07:05.696 --> 07:09.116
‎If Doctor X never leaves a patient's side,

88
07:09.909 --> 07:11.827
‎then she's Doctor X.

89
07:12.703 --> 07:15.164
‎If Doctor X does their best

90
07:15.248 --> 07:18.000
‎to carry out every surgery ‎assigned to them,

91
07:18.084 --> 07:19.794
‎then she's Doctor X.

92
07:20.670 --> 07:23.506
‎If a doctor who never fails is Doctor X,

93
07:24.257 --> 07:25.132
‎then you're right.

94
07:26.259 --> 07:28.886
‎Gye Su-jeong is most certainly Doctor X.

95
07:29.595 --> 07:30.555
‎Ms. Jang.

96
07:30.638 --> 07:32.598
‎This hospital is losing ‎patients and staff.

97
07:32.682 --> 07:34.976
‎What is there to gain by doubting a doctor

98
07:35.059 --> 07:38.062
‎who is doing everything ‎to save her patient?

99
07:38.145 --> 07:40.731
‎The patient died a month after surgery.

100
07:40.815 --> 07:42.858
‎But Mr. Park Gwang-cheol is alive.

101
07:42.942 --> 07:44.777
‎And he's recovering very nicely.

102
07:52.076 --> 07:53.202
‎Have you forgotten

103
07:53.286 --> 07:56.956
‎who helped secure your current position?

104
07:58.791 --> 08:00.501
‎I have this.

105
08:01.460 --> 08:04.005
‎Did you put what I gave you to good use?

106
08:04.088 --> 08:06.591
‎Then we'll save that for next time.

107
08:08.926 --> 08:12.096
‎Is this the occasion ‎you saved that card up for?

108
08:14.223 --> 08:15.558
‎Of course not.

109
08:16.434 --> 08:17.935
‎I can't waste a card like that

110
08:18.477 --> 08:20.396
‎over a baseless accusation.

111
08:21.897 --> 08:22.982
‎"Baseless"?

112
08:25.067 --> 08:28.029
‎If I start looking into Dr. Gye--

113
08:28.112 --> 08:29.405
‎It's glaucoma, isn't it?

114
08:31.949 --> 08:33.993
‎Your vision isn't completely impaired,

115
08:34.744 --> 08:37.455
‎so why didn't you operate on ‎Ms. Yeo Jeong-sun?

116
08:41.292 --> 08:42.293
‎I see.

117
08:43.044 --> 08:44.837
‎Instead of losing your peripheral vision,

118
08:46.297 --> 08:47.923
‎your central vision is going first.

119
08:50.092 --> 08:52.094
‎What's your point?

120
08:52.178 --> 08:55.014
‎Don't you want to know how I found out?

121
08:55.848 --> 08:57.892
‎I got curious.

122
08:57.975 --> 09:01.228
‎They used to call you the hands of God.

123
09:01.312 --> 09:03.397
‎So why did you put down your scalpel

124
09:03.481 --> 09:05.733
‎and get your hands dirty in politics?

125
09:11.072 --> 09:12.948
‎You have too much time on your hands.

126
09:13.574 --> 09:14.992
‎Don't you have better things to do?

127
09:15.826 --> 09:16.702
‎Ms. Jang.

128
09:17.995 --> 09:18.871
‎This is what you call

129
09:19.789 --> 09:21.749
‎coming up empty-handed.

130
09:25.336 --> 09:26.420
‎Gye Su-jeong

131
09:27.838 --> 09:29.882
‎is Doctor X.

132
09:32.843 --> 09:36.889
‎A doctor who takes on high-risk cases ‎with no standard surgical procedures.

133
09:40.768 --> 09:41.769
‎Beginning hilum dissection.

134
09:41.852 --> 09:44.313
‎HILUM DISSECTION: DISSECTING TISSUE ‎AROUND AN ORGAN'S ENTRY OR EXIT POINT

135
09:44.397 --> 09:48.901
‎Or an exceptional yet arrogant surgeon ‎who enjoys putting her skills to the test

136
09:49.527 --> 09:51.404
‎with a patient's life ‎hanging in the balance.

137
09:56.158 --> 09:57.910
‎Hang in there, Ga-eul.

138
10:03.457 --> 10:06.585
‎A name where respect and cynicism coexist.

139
10:11.257 --> 10:12.883
‎You're already at that phase?

140
10:13.384 --> 10:15.177
‎Guess you didn't need me.

141
10:15.261 --> 10:17.513
‎Wow, things must have moved pretty fast.

142
10:17.596 --> 10:18.848
‎Why are you here?

143
10:18.931 --> 10:21.600
‎I came to assist ‎and watch Dr. Gye operate.

144
10:21.684 --> 10:22.727
‎He came running.

145
10:23.602 --> 10:25.062
‎Give me a hand when I tie it up later.

146
10:25.146 --> 10:26.272
‎-I will. ‎-Not you.

147
10:26.856 --> 10:30.234
‎Right. Ms. Go is much better than me.

148
10:30.776 --> 10:31.944
‎Next, the posteroinferior region.

149
10:32.027 --> 10:33.571
‎Already? Seriously?

150
10:33.654 --> 10:35.322
‎She's serious. It'll be soon.

151
10:35.406 --> 10:37.366
‎We need to identify ‎and preserve the right ureter,

152
10:37.450 --> 10:39.410
‎-so page urology right now. ‎-Yes, Doctor.

153
10:41.912 --> 10:46.417
‎That's what I think Doctor X means.

154
10:46.500 --> 10:47.334
‎In which case…

155
10:48.961 --> 10:50.212
‎Gye Su-jeong is‎…

156
10:52.006 --> 10:54.091
‎Doctor X in my book.

157
10:59.221 --> 11:00.181
‎Damn it.

158
11:05.603 --> 11:10.232
‎You're nothing but a director ‎at Guseo University's branch hospital.

159
11:11.692 --> 11:13.360
‎What good does it do you to know

160
11:14.069 --> 11:15.613
‎who Gye Su-jeong is

161
11:17.072 --> 11:19.116
‎or who Doctor X is?

162
11:23.120 --> 11:24.955
‎She escaped ‎and barely got back on her feet…

163
11:27.374 --> 11:28.918
‎and is hanging on by a thread.

164
11:30.127 --> 11:33.923
‎She's trying so hard to save lives, ‎yet you want to dig into her past?

165
11:34.507 --> 11:35.382
‎And for what?

166
11:36.550 --> 11:37.968
‎What the hell are you going to do?

167
11:54.068 --> 11:57.112
‎I didn't know you'd fly solo ‎without the other departments.

168
11:57.196 --> 11:58.697
‎When I'm needed, I step up.

169
11:58.781 --> 12:00.658
‎Dr. Gye is pretty amazing, right?

170
12:06.163 --> 12:07.289
‎I'll do that, Dr. Gye.

171
12:07.873 --> 12:09.708
‎It's the least I can do.

172
12:10.251 --> 12:11.710
‎Don't you have to go?

173
12:11.794 --> 12:14.004
‎You finished so quickly ‎that I have time to spare.

174
12:14.672 --> 12:17.299
‎You have 40 minutes left ‎until you clock out, Dr. Gye.

175
12:17.383 --> 12:19.510
‎And I have 40 minutes left ‎until my next surgery.

176
12:21.178 --> 12:22.638
‎I have extra time too.

177
12:26.308 --> 12:29.103
‎Dr. Gye has to do this part herself too.

178
12:29.186 --> 12:30.187
‎It's okay.

179
12:42.908 --> 12:45.202
‎Good job, Dr. Gye.

180
12:46.370 --> 12:47.329
‎Good job.

181
12:52.835 --> 12:54.878
‎She looks peaceful.

182
12:55.963 --> 12:57.631
‎Ga-eul doesn't seem to be in pain.

183
12:57.715 --> 12:58.882
‎A doctor shouldn't say that.

184
12:59.466 --> 13:01.594
‎Dr. Park, you're just asking for trouble.

185
13:33.584 --> 13:35.336
‎Good night, Dr. Gye.

186
13:51.018 --> 13:53.979
‎12 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

187
13:55.814 --> 13:58.525
‎My little puppy, Ga-eul…

188
13:59.985 --> 14:00.986
‎Can you hear me?

189
14:02.196 --> 14:04.031
‎Don't fall asleep.

190
14:04.865 --> 14:07.785
‎This is a surprise. ‎What brings you here, Dr. Jo?

191
14:08.827 --> 14:10.829
‎I had to come and check.

192
14:12.623 --> 14:14.416
‎Even Dr. Jo is here.

193
14:14.500 --> 14:16.919
‎Where's the primary surgeon?

194
14:18.754 --> 14:20.255
‎She went to a bathhouse.

195
14:21.382 --> 14:24.051
‎She even borrowed 1,500 won from me ‎to buy banana milk.

196
14:25.052 --> 14:27.388
‎I gave her 2,000 won ‎since I had no change, and she ran off.

197
14:28.013 --> 14:29.098
‎Jeez.

198
14:30.057 --> 14:32.351
‎Seriously? A bathhouse?

199
14:32.434 --> 14:34.895
‎Man, banana milk?

200
14:34.979 --> 14:36.230
‎Lucky her for clocking out.

201
14:37.189 --> 14:38.107
‎Goodness.

202
14:38.899 --> 14:42.403
‎All the attendings are still here ‎in case something happens,

203
14:43.320 --> 14:44.863
‎but this can't continue.

204
14:46.073 --> 14:47.992
‎They'll change their minds soon.

205
14:48.075 --> 14:50.411
‎I'm sure this won't last long.

206
14:50.911 --> 14:52.955
‎It didn't drag on back then either.

207
14:53.038 --> 14:54.790
‎But that was during COVID-19.

208
14:55.874 --> 14:58.711
‎-Who knows what'll happen this time? ‎-The doors are opening.

209
15:01.588 --> 15:02.423
‎-Hey! ‎-Hello.

210
15:03.090 --> 15:05.634
‎I almost didn't recognize you ‎without your white coat.

211
15:06.135 --> 15:07.845
‎I took it off temporarily. I haven't…

212
15:07.928 --> 15:09.555
‎Waiting until it's time to clear out?

213
15:09.638 --> 15:10.806
‎Yes, sir.

214
15:10.889 --> 15:14.059
‎Right, you always see things through.

215
15:14.143 --> 15:16.937
‎Of course. He's Ma Seong-cute, after all.

216
15:17.021 --> 15:19.440
‎He's a good doctor and works hard.

217
15:31.577 --> 15:33.996
‎-Go ahead and take care of things. ‎-Yes, sir.

218
15:34.079 --> 15:37.082
‎You're coming back ‎for the emergency meeting vote, right?

219
15:37.166 --> 15:38.459
‎-Yes, of course. ‎-Good.

220
15:38.542 --> 15:39.501
‎Bye.

221
15:41.211 --> 15:42.212
‎Hey.

222
15:43.630 --> 15:44.882
‎Answer your phone, punk.

223
15:47.426 --> 15:48.260
‎Yes, sir.

224
15:49.219 --> 15:50.846
‎All right, take care.

225
15:55.809 --> 15:59.396
‎I didn't recognize him ‎without his white coat.

226
15:59.480 --> 16:02.024
‎It took him three tries ‎to get into med school.

227
16:02.107 --> 16:04.777
‎The youngest son of a single mother ‎who runs a pharmacy.

228
16:07.279 --> 16:08.405
‎Remember the day

229
16:09.198 --> 16:11.700
‎we started calling him "Ma Seong-cute"?

230
16:12.201 --> 16:13.118
‎2 YEARS AGO

231
16:13.202 --> 16:14.328
‎My mom…

232
16:15.412 --> 16:16.872
‎She wants me to work my way up

233
16:16.955 --> 16:19.374
‎and become an attending here, ‎not open a private practice.

234
16:19.458 --> 16:20.709
‎-I see. ‎-Really?

235
16:20.793 --> 16:23.754
‎The doctor above the pharmacy ‎put her through hell.

236
16:24.797 --> 16:27.841
‎But I… I really want to become a doctor.

237
16:27.925 --> 16:30.219
‎I seriously want to become a doctor.

238
16:31.470 --> 16:33.055
‎Seung-gwon, my bro!

239
16:33.138 --> 16:36.475
‎-Want to see a photo of my cute niece? ‎-Hey, Seong-gyu.

240
16:36.558 --> 16:38.685
‎Cute! Isn't she super cute?

241
16:38.769 --> 16:40.145
‎She's so cute.

242
16:40.229 --> 16:41.355
‎Cute.

243
16:41.438 --> 16:42.773
‎I'm cute too, right?

244
16:42.856 --> 16:44.233
‎Cute!

245
16:44.316 --> 16:45.859
‎Tell me I'm cute.

246
16:46.443 --> 16:47.402
‎You're cute too.

247
16:47.486 --> 16:49.488
‎You're cute too, bro. You really can eat.

248
16:49.571 --> 16:51.949
‎-You're so cute, bro. ‎-How cute.

249
16:52.991 --> 16:53.867
‎It'll end soon.

250
16:54.910 --> 16:58.914
‎If they take away the clinical hours ‎interns and residents badly need…

251
16:59.665 --> 17:01.083
‎No way they'd want to risk that.

252
17:01.583 --> 17:03.460
‎It'll get sorted out ‎by the end of this week.

253
17:04.711 --> 17:05.838
‎The doors are opening.

254
17:19.476 --> 17:20.310
‎This is just…

255
17:32.239 --> 17:33.532
‎Goodness.

256
17:34.116 --> 17:37.744
‎I can't believe Eung-gu ‎is treating us to pizza.

257
17:37.828 --> 17:38.954
‎Here.

258
17:39.621 --> 17:41.540
‎Congratulations on getting hired, Eung-gu.

259
17:42.166 --> 17:44.376
‎This is my first time buying pizza too.

260
17:44.459 --> 17:46.587
‎I hear it's good. Su-jeong, eat up.

261
17:46.670 --> 17:50.382
‎Try the one with corn ‎and shrimp toppings, Su-jeong.

262
17:50.465 --> 17:51.884
‎Sweet and spicy in one bite, right?

263
17:54.136 --> 17:55.220
‎All right.

264
17:55.888 --> 17:57.723
‎-Congrats! ‎-Goodness.

265
18:02.895 --> 18:06.273
‎Guseo University Medical Center ‎is still afloat, thanks to Su-jeong.

266
18:06.356 --> 18:07.900
‎Ms. Jang.

267
18:08.734 --> 18:09.651
‎You'll make a pretty penny.

268
18:09.735 --> 18:11.445
‎Then can I get 2,000 won later?

269
18:14.698 --> 18:16.408
‎Ms. Jang, you're quiet today.

270
18:16.491 --> 18:17.701
‎You're not eating either.

271
18:18.994 --> 18:21.413
‎Director Bu brought up Doctor X.

272
18:22.539 --> 18:23.832
‎How much does he know?

273
18:23.916 --> 18:25.042
‎He only read the article.

274
18:25.125 --> 18:26.627
‎He was just testing me.

275
18:26.710 --> 18:29.296
‎I hit him back pretty hard, ‎but I still feel uneasy.

276
18:29.379 --> 18:32.341
‎We haven't said that name to each other…

277
18:32.424 --> 18:33.717
‎In ages, yes.

278
18:35.010 --> 18:36.595
‎Not happy to hear it.

279
18:38.180 --> 18:40.807
‎We need to walk away from this hospital.

280
18:41.516 --> 18:42.643
‎No.

281
18:54.655 --> 18:55.656
‎I need to do this surgery.

282
18:56.698 --> 18:58.617
‎"Lee Hyeon-a, eight years old."

283
18:58.700 --> 19:00.744
‎MALIGNANT NEOPLASM ‎OF CONNECTIVE &amp; SOFT TISSUE OF ABDOMEN

284
19:13.632 --> 19:15.092
‎Malignant myofibroblastic tumor?

285
19:15.175 --> 19:18.428
‎I know IMTs usually present in children,

286
19:19.096 --> 19:21.098
‎but this transformation…

287
19:22.099 --> 19:24.309
‎I've only read about it. ‎I've never seen it firsthand.

288
19:26.353 --> 19:28.313
‎This is an extremely rare case.

289
19:29.231 --> 19:30.107
‎It measures 15 cm

290
19:30.983 --> 19:32.901
‎and encases the abdominal aorta.

291
19:35.696 --> 19:38.282
‎Why are you Western doctors sighing?

292
19:38.365 --> 19:39.491
‎Fill me in, will you?

293
19:42.119 --> 19:43.745
‎Surgery is impossible, Su-jeong.

294
19:44.454 --> 19:46.123
‎There's no procedure for this.

295
19:46.206 --> 19:47.833
‎-I'll find a way. ‎-No.

296
19:49.626 --> 19:50.460
‎Why not?

297
19:50.544 --> 19:53.380
‎It'll make you look more like Doctor X.

298
20:06.310 --> 20:07.436
‎You got a letter.

299
20:12.190 --> 20:13.984
‎If you won't reply, at least read it.

300
20:22.826 --> 20:24.453
‎She can't even read this letter.

301
20:26.955 --> 20:28.665
‎It's not like this will bring him back.

302
20:43.472 --> 20:44.306
‎No.

303
20:45.140 --> 20:46.141
‎There must be a way.

304
20:47.893 --> 20:49.144
‎Get it together.

305
20:52.064 --> 20:52.898
‎Eat while you work.

306
20:55.233 --> 20:56.234
‎Here.

307
21:09.456 --> 21:10.999
‎Thank you, Eung-gu.

308
21:11.083 --> 21:12.709
‎You know where she's coming from, right?

309
21:15.879 --> 21:19.299
‎Everyone in this house ‎is haunted by the past.

310
21:22.761 --> 21:24.888
‎They say there's no paradise to escape to,

311
21:26.098 --> 21:27.057
‎but sometimes,

312
21:27.849 --> 21:28.975
‎I feel happy here.

313
21:30.727 --> 21:31.603
‎Even though I shouldn't.

314
21:34.398 --> 21:36.108
‎Me, your aunt, and Mi-gyeong.

315
21:37.234 --> 21:40.862
‎We're all afraid we'll lose you again.

316
21:42.322 --> 21:43.198
‎The older you get,

317
21:44.366 --> 21:45.909
‎the more afraid you get.

318
21:50.247 --> 21:51.248
‎Still,

319
21:52.499 --> 21:53.792
‎this child's life is more important.

320
21:55.794 --> 21:58.713
‎My word, my kid was this age once.

321
22:02.134 --> 22:05.220
‎If she were alive, ‎she'd be an adult by now.

322
22:08.640 --> 22:11.435
‎I hope we can see this kid grow up.

323
22:15.355 --> 22:16.940
‎Find a way.

324
22:17.524 --> 22:20.152
‎You can do it, Gye Su-jeong.

325
22:35.917 --> 22:38.044
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

326
22:40.839 --> 22:41.798
‎Dr. Gye…

327
22:42.424 --> 22:43.341
‎What the heck?

328
22:44.217 --> 22:46.553
‎Why isn't she here?

329
22:46.636 --> 22:47.846
‎Where is she?

330
22:47.929 --> 22:49.890
‎Don't tell me she went on strike too?

331
22:54.519 --> 22:55.687
‎Oh, I know.

332
22:59.941 --> 23:00.775
‎What's this?

333
23:04.029 --> 23:04.946
‎Dr. Park.

334
23:05.697 --> 23:06.698
‎Dr. Park?

335
23:07.324 --> 23:09.826
‎Am I unable to wake you, ‎or are you pretending to be asleep?

336
23:10.577 --> 23:12.329
‎Wake up, Dr. Park.

337
23:13.788 --> 23:14.706
‎Dr. Kim.

338
23:15.540 --> 23:16.499
‎I'm sorry.

339
23:17.125 --> 23:20.128
‎I couldn't find a place for a quick nap,

340
23:20.629 --> 23:22.589
‎so I dozed off a bit…

341
23:22.672 --> 23:24.549
‎There are plenty of places to take a nap,

342
23:24.633 --> 23:26.801
‎like the surgical staff room ‎and the on-call room.

343
23:27.427 --> 23:30.222
‎But no one's there.

344
23:30.305 --> 23:32.015
‎So what if no one's there?

345
23:32.098 --> 23:33.642
‎He's scared because no one's there.

346
23:34.226 --> 23:35.560
‎The ER can't take patients,

347
23:35.644 --> 23:37.771
‎but at least doctors and nurses walk by.

348
23:37.854 --> 23:39.981
‎This isn't some kind of a hostel.

349
23:40.065 --> 23:41.524
‎Listen, you punk.

350
23:41.608 --> 23:43.777
‎The ER is closed, but we still--

351
23:43.860 --> 23:44.986
‎But today,

352
23:45.070 --> 23:47.322
‎Director Bu and the attendings are here,

353
23:47.405 --> 23:48.782
‎so can't you open the ER?

354
23:49.532 --> 23:51.117
‎It doesn't matter if they're here.

355
23:51.201 --> 23:54.537
‎We still can't take patients ‎due to lack of definitive care.

356
23:54.621 --> 23:57.207
‎Sorry for bringing you down ‎first thing in the morning.

357
24:00.418 --> 24:03.338
‎Then buy me a coffee, ‎a sandwich, and ice cream.

358
24:03.421 --> 24:04.381
‎For him too.

359
24:04.464 --> 24:06.132
‎Oh, I'm fine.

360
24:06.216 --> 24:08.468
‎I really need to snap out of it,

361
24:08.551 --> 24:10.220
‎but I've been dragging my feet.

362
24:10.303 --> 24:12.389
‎-I'll get some fresh air outside… ‎-No.

363
24:12.472 --> 24:14.057
‎You'll get caught if you go outside.

364
24:14.140 --> 24:15.100
‎What?

365
24:16.101 --> 24:17.769
‎You know, I've been thinking…

366
24:19.104 --> 24:22.148
‎We should've sold ‎gimbap ‎at the front gate.

367
24:22.232 --> 24:23.775
‎Not to patients, but to the reporters.

368
24:25.527 --> 24:27.862
‎That money could've covered ‎multiple work dinners.

369
24:29.030 --> 24:30.198
‎I guess it started.

370
24:31.199 --> 24:34.077
‎WORK STOPPAGE BEGINS

371
24:41.126 --> 24:42.794
‎NOTICE FOR PATIENTS AND THEIR FAMILIES

372
24:44.754 --> 24:46.298
‎INTERN RESIDENT STRIKE VOTE COMMITTEE

373
24:59.144 --> 25:01.896
‎Dr. Ma, I got a nosebleed ‎and got some blood on this page,

374
25:01.980 --> 25:03.481
‎but I couldn't wipe it off.

375
25:03.565 --> 25:06.526
‎I was afraid of tearing a hole in it, ‎so I covered it up with this note.

376
25:06.609 --> 25:07.527
‎I'm sorry.

377
25:07.610 --> 25:09.821
‎By the way, there was a nosebleed stain ‎on the back too.

378
25:11.448 --> 25:13.616
‎It made me feel better for some reason,

379
25:13.700 --> 25:16.828
‎knowing that you, Dr. Ma Seong-cute, ‎are also human.

380
25:16.911 --> 25:18.621
‎Thank you for lending me your book.

381
25:18.705 --> 25:20.623
‎And thank you for your nosebleed.

382
25:21.875 --> 25:24.753
‎I know you'll become a great doctor.

383
25:32.844 --> 25:35.013
‎Why did this punk scribble in my book?

384
25:40.769 --> 25:44.272
‎YEAR 2020

385
25:49.277 --> 25:50.653
‎You know I don't have the time.

386
25:50.737 --> 25:53.782
‎Surgeries are all backed up ‎because of COVID-19 and the strike.

387
25:54.741 --> 25:55.700
‎Tell them to sue me.

388
25:56.242 --> 25:57.994
‎I did my best with that surgery.

389
25:59.454 --> 26:00.663
‎All right, bye.

390
26:11.049 --> 26:12.842
‎Hello? Hey.

391
26:13.676 --> 26:16.429
‎Bring me a new mask. ‎I'm in the restroom by the staff room.

392
26:16.513 --> 26:17.972
‎I have an emergency surgery.

393
26:18.598 --> 26:19.432
‎Okay.

394
26:23.228 --> 26:25.230
‎Did you take a PCR test?

395
26:25.313 --> 26:26.564
‎-Negative? ‎-Yes, sir.

396
26:27.565 --> 26:28.483
‎Here, sir.

397
26:29.067 --> 26:29.943
‎It's new.

398
26:30.693 --> 26:31.778
‎Why?

399
26:31.861 --> 26:33.405
‎You can't walk the hallways without one.

400
26:33.488 --> 26:34.781
‎You're in a hurry, right?

401
26:34.864 --> 26:35.782
‎Right.

402
26:36.282 --> 26:37.700
‎-Then take it. ‎-What about you?

403
26:38.284 --> 26:40.412
‎I'll take the one ‎from the person you called.

404
26:41.037 --> 26:42.872
‎Oh, that's…

405
26:43.915 --> 26:45.333
‎-Thanks. ‎-You're welcome.

406
26:46.543 --> 26:47.377
‎Thanks.

407
26:48.586 --> 26:49.421
‎What's your name?

408
26:49.504 --> 26:51.047
‎It's Ma Seong-gyu, sir.

409
26:51.131 --> 26:52.382
‎I see.

410
26:53.133 --> 26:55.218
‎Na Seon-gyun. Thanks.

411
26:57.887 --> 27:00.348
‎DR. MA SEONG-GYU

412
27:16.823 --> 27:19.325
‎DR. MA SEONG-GYU

413
27:23.788 --> 27:24.622
‎Dr. Ma.

414
27:25.457 --> 27:28.501
‎The Ministry of Health and Welfare ‎sent a return-to-work order text.

415
27:28.585 --> 27:30.670
‎A return-to-work order text?

416
27:30.962 --> 27:32.255
‎RETURN-TO-WORK ORDER

417
27:33.506 --> 27:34.340
‎REPERCUSSIONS INCLUDE…

418
27:34.424 --> 27:35.300
‎"License revocation"?

419
27:36.301 --> 27:37.260
‎I'll see you later, sir.

420
27:37.969 --> 27:38.803
‎Okay.

421
27:52.484 --> 27:54.486
‎7:50 A.M. ‎WEDNESDAY, APRIL 29

422
27:58.031 --> 27:59.199
‎Man…

423
28:05.288 --> 28:06.623
‎-Look. ‎-There he is.

424
28:06.706 --> 28:08.625
‎-It's him. ‎-Hurry.

425
28:08.708 --> 28:10.460
‎Are you leaving the hospital?

426
28:10.543 --> 28:12.337
‎Are you really joining the work stoppage?

427
28:12.420 --> 28:13.254
‎Yes, that's right.

428
28:13.338 --> 28:15.924
‎What's the current ‎work stoppage participation rate?

429
28:16.007 --> 28:18.176
‎It's about 85% at our hospital alone.

430
28:18.259 --> 28:20.178
‎Any words as the association chapter head?

431
28:20.845 --> 28:21.721
‎Well…

432
28:22.639 --> 28:25.892
‎I'm deeply sorry that we have to ‎leave the hospital today.

433
28:25.975 --> 28:27.727
‎I'm sure everyone feels the same.

434
28:27.810 --> 28:29.604
‎The government sent ‎mass text notifications

435
28:29.687 --> 28:31.439
‎announcing legal measures.

436
28:31.523 --> 28:35.443
‎To continue our fight, ‎we plan to tender our resignations…

437
28:35.527 --> 28:37.028
‎Letters of resignation?

438
28:38.279 --> 28:39.948
‎This vote will be held during…

439
28:40.031 --> 28:43.952
‎-This is going to last a while. ‎-Residents, interns, and even attendings…

440
28:44.035 --> 28:46.162
‎Shouldn't we discuss this with Magnolia?

441
28:46.246 --> 28:48.039
‎There's no point

442
28:48.122 --> 28:51.084
‎since Magnolia is backing this fight.

443
28:52.585 --> 28:54.087
‎However, if this continues…

444
28:55.755 --> 28:58.091
‎they'll bring up ‎closing the hospital again.

445
28:59.634 --> 29:00.510
‎Come in.

446
29:00.593 --> 29:03.012
‎This strike is a last resort ‎to prevent healthcare collapse.

447
29:03.096 --> 29:04.639
‎We are stepping up

448
29:04.722 --> 29:07.725
‎to protect patients from a government ‎that pushes a market logic

449
29:07.809 --> 29:09.227
‎centered on major hospitals…

450
29:09.310 --> 29:12.063
‎What brings you here so early, Dr. Gye?

451
29:14.774 --> 29:17.235
‎"The locum is allowed to perform ‎the surgery she wants."

452
29:18.444 --> 29:19.654
‎It's my contract term.

453
29:24.409 --> 29:27.287
‎MALIGNANT NEOPLASM ‎OF CONNECTIVE &amp; SOFT TISSUE OF ABDOMEN

454
29:27.370 --> 29:28.997
‎There's no surgical procedure--

455
29:29.080 --> 29:32.292
‎You said if I pulled off ‎Yoo Ga-eul's surgery in six hours,

456
29:32.792 --> 29:35.962
‎you'd be more flexible with this term.

457
29:37.005 --> 29:38.673
‎It took 5 hours and 20 minutes.

458
29:38.756 --> 29:41.593
‎So, is this one of those?

459
29:42.176 --> 29:43.136
‎Yes.

460
29:43.845 --> 29:46.890
‎No, this patient has already been ‎cleared for discharge.

461
29:47.390 --> 29:49.058
‎Do you know this case, Dr. Do?

462
29:49.142 --> 29:51.144
‎We were requested to consult on it,

463
29:52.270 --> 29:54.355
‎but it seemed hopeless, ‎so we declined the case.

464
29:55.023 --> 29:57.901
‎The main hospital thought so too, ‎which is why they transferred her here.

465
29:57.984 --> 30:01.529
‎But Dr. Gye thinks ‎the patient has a chance.

466
30:02.363 --> 30:03.197
‎I want to operate.

467
30:03.781 --> 30:05.116
‎You can't. This is--

468
30:05.199 --> 30:06.034
‎Understood.

469
30:10.955 --> 30:12.457
‎Let's hold a pre-op conference.

470
30:18.671 --> 30:20.673
‎Persuade the other doctors.

471
30:21.674 --> 30:23.009
‎CASE 1: LEE HYEON-A, F/8

472
30:23.092 --> 30:26.512
‎I called this conference on short notice ‎at a special request.

473
30:26.596 --> 30:28.681
‎Of the remaining staff,

474
30:28.765 --> 30:31.392
‎I invited only those doctors ‎who can assist with this surgery,

475
30:31.476 --> 30:32.518
‎so please listen closely.

476
30:33.102 --> 30:35.647
‎Director Bu, this surgery…

477
30:35.730 --> 30:36.648
‎Who…

478
30:37.273 --> 30:38.441
‎Who's the primary surgeon?

479
30:39.233 --> 30:40.652
‎It's Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

480
30:44.238 --> 30:45.907
‎The patient is Lee Hyeon-a.

481
30:45.990 --> 30:47.283
‎She is eight years old

482
30:47.367 --> 30:49.077
‎and has a malignant myofibroblastic tumor.

483
30:50.161 --> 30:52.038
‎It has invaded the caudate lobe, IVC,

484
30:52.121 --> 30:53.790
‎head of the pancreas, portal vein,

485
30:53.873 --> 30:55.959
‎SMV, SMA,

486
30:56.042 --> 30:58.378
‎and even the mesocolon.

487
30:58.461 --> 30:59.837
‎We declined the case

488
30:59.921 --> 31:02.632
‎since the tumor was so extensive ‎and in a bad spot.

489
31:02.715 --> 31:03.633
‎You're right.

490
31:04.717 --> 31:06.344
‎It's very bad.

491
31:10.181 --> 31:13.851
‎She has three months left at most.

492
31:15.520 --> 31:19.190
‎Dr. Gye, everyone here feels terrible ‎about her limited time.

493
31:19.273 --> 31:21.484
‎-But-- ‎-The tumor measures 15 cm.

494
31:21.567 --> 31:23.611
‎Major arteries are involved,

495
31:23.695 --> 31:25.154
‎so we'd have to cut off blood flow.

496
31:25.238 --> 31:26.572
‎This is inoperable.

497
31:26.656 --> 31:28.574
‎There's literally no surgical procedure.

498
31:28.658 --> 31:30.952
‎Yes, there is a procedure.

499
31:37.208 --> 31:40.670
‎We'll do a multivisceral ‎ex vivo tumor resection

500
31:40.753 --> 31:42.005
‎and autotransplantation.

501
31:42.797 --> 31:45.174
‎Multi… auto… what?

502
31:47.343 --> 31:49.220
‎A total of six organs,

503
31:49.303 --> 31:53.141
‎including the stomach, pancreas, ‎spleen, liver, large intestine,

504
31:53.224 --> 31:54.517
‎and small intestine,

505
31:55.351 --> 31:57.603
‎are removed from the body ‎along with the tumor.

506
32:03.901 --> 32:05.403
‎Is that even possible?

507
32:05.486 --> 32:06.988
‎Does that surgery actually exist?

508
32:07.071 --> 32:08.656
‎No, it doesn't.

509
32:09.532 --> 32:10.658
‎I've never heard of it.

510
32:10.742 --> 32:13.828
‎Removing this tumor in its original place

511
32:14.328 --> 32:19.250
‎would take too long since it encases ‎multiple organs and vessels.

512
32:19.751 --> 32:21.210
‎Without blood flow,

513
32:21.294 --> 32:22.670
‎the organs will become necrotic.

514
32:22.754 --> 32:25.965
‎We know that, Dr. Gye. But we can't just--

515
32:26.049 --> 32:26.883
‎In short,

516
32:26.966 --> 32:30.428
‎we extract all organs from the abdomen,

517
32:30.511 --> 32:32.138
‎resect the tumor,

518
32:32.221 --> 32:33.848
‎and then put them back in.

519
32:33.931 --> 32:37.477
‎You're looking at this ‎like it's a standard organ transplant…

520
32:37.560 --> 32:38.394
‎You're right.

521
32:40.104 --> 32:43.941
‎How many blood vessels ‎are you planning to cut and reconnect?

522
32:44.025 --> 32:45.109
‎Probably a lot.

523
32:45.193 --> 32:47.445
‎-Are you insane, Dr. Gye? ‎-How long?

524
32:50.364 --> 32:51.282
‎Fifteen hours.

525
32:51.866 --> 32:53.117
‎Fifteen hours?

526
32:53.951 --> 32:55.870
‎It takes six hours ‎just to put two back in.

527
32:55.953 --> 32:57.955
‎Listen to yourself.

528
32:58.039 --> 32:59.791
‎It won't work. It's too risky, sir.

529
32:59.874 --> 33:00.750
‎Yes.

530
33:01.584 --> 33:03.127
‎It's a very risky surgery.

531
33:03.211 --> 33:04.420
‎Have you done this before?

532
33:04.962 --> 33:06.464
‎You're speaking from experience, right?

533
33:07.381 --> 33:08.633
‎No.

534
33:08.716 --> 33:11.761
‎You're proposing a procedure ‎you've never done before?

535
33:11.844 --> 33:13.596
‎This is bound to fail.

536
33:13.679 --> 33:15.431
‎I bet everyone here agrees with me.

537
33:26.275 --> 33:27.985
‎Hey, why aren't you saying it?

538
33:28.778 --> 33:31.447
‎Your catchphrase. "I don't fail."

539
33:33.116 --> 33:33.991
‎Why won't you say it?

540
33:43.417 --> 33:44.502
‎I need a team.

541
33:53.052 --> 33:54.804
‎Once the six organs are exteriorized,

542
33:54.887 --> 33:57.098
‎they are kept chilled ‎in preservation solution

543
33:57.181 --> 33:59.600
‎while the team ‎resects the tumor on the bench

544
34:00.184 --> 34:02.728
‎and performs vascular reconstruction.

545
34:05.273 --> 34:08.818
‎The child can only hold on for so long,

546
34:09.360 --> 34:13.447
‎so the surgeons need to team up ‎and work simultaneously to save time.

547
34:13.531 --> 34:15.908
‎We replace tumor-invaded vessels ‎with synthetic ones,

548
34:15.992 --> 34:18.202
‎then re-implant the organs

549
34:18.286 --> 34:20.329
‎and restore blood flow.

550
34:21.831 --> 34:25.376
‎What if there's extensive tumor invasion ‎extending to the tail of the pancreas?

551
34:25.459 --> 34:26.294
‎Then what?

552
34:26.377 --> 34:27.837
‎We remove the entire pancreas.

553
34:28.588 --> 34:31.299
‎But we'll run biopsies ‎during surgery to prevent--

554
34:31.382 --> 34:32.884
‎We'll take this to the IRB.

555
34:37.054 --> 34:39.265
‎Any new surgical procedure

556
34:39.348 --> 34:41.350
‎must be approved by the IRB.

557
34:41.434 --> 34:43.352
‎It's not an entirely new procedure.

558
34:43.436 --> 34:47.273
‎Unprecedented procedures ‎need IRB approval.

559
34:47.940 --> 34:49.609
‎Compile the surgery files,

560
34:49.692 --> 34:51.235
‎get patient consent, and submit them.

561
34:51.861 --> 34:53.154
‎How long will an approval take?

562
34:53.237 --> 34:55.239
‎It usually takes a week, so just wait.

563
34:55.323 --> 34:57.783
‎That's too late. We can't wait.

564
34:58.618 --> 34:59.535
‎Dr. Gye.

565
35:01.621 --> 35:04.665
‎Do you think anyone will take part?

566
35:06.584 --> 35:08.836
‎This surgery is practically a gamble.

567
35:08.920 --> 35:11.547
‎Are you putting ‎an eight-year-old's life on the line

568
35:11.631 --> 35:12.924
‎and risking not only yours

569
35:13.633 --> 35:16.052
‎but other people's careers as well?

570
35:19.931 --> 35:23.809
‎I'm putting my reputation ‎as a surgeon on the line

571
35:25.019 --> 35:27.980
‎to save the life ‎of an eight-year-old patient.

572
35:28.940 --> 35:29.941
‎Then wait.

573
35:30.775 --> 35:32.526
‎Don't you need a team

574
35:32.610 --> 35:35.154
‎and an OR you can use all day?

575
35:36.280 --> 35:38.241
‎Follow protocol, ‎and once you get approval--

576
35:38.324 --> 35:39.242
‎That child

577
35:39.909 --> 35:41.410
‎has no time.

578
35:42.536 --> 35:44.247
‎Then how about two days from now?

579
35:46.040 --> 35:47.416
‎That's definitely a day

580
35:47.500 --> 35:50.795
‎you can operate in the main OR all day.

581
35:50.878 --> 35:52.838
‎All other ORs are available that day too.

582
35:55.007 --> 35:58.636
‎It's the day of the strike rally ‎and the hospital-wide resignation vote.

583
35:59.679 --> 36:02.014
‎I assume everyone got this text

584
36:02.098 --> 36:03.391
‎except for Dr. Gye.

585
36:04.558 --> 36:08.354
‎You're all going to the rally ‎to join the strike, right?

586
36:11.357 --> 36:13.150
‎Let me ask everyone now.

587
36:16.362 --> 36:17.196
‎Now then.

588
36:18.239 --> 36:20.616
‎Are there any attendings here

589
36:22.159 --> 36:23.661
‎willing to scrub in as lead surgeons?

590
36:35.840 --> 36:37.091
‎Submit the documents first.

591
36:38.551 --> 36:40.636
‎Let's buy some time to persuade them.

592
36:40.720 --> 36:41.887
‎Right now,

593
36:42.471 --> 36:43.931
‎no one here will raise their hand.

594
36:52.064 --> 36:54.108
‎These people won't come.

595
36:55.735 --> 36:57.445
‎The IRB and the strike aren't the problem.

596
36:58.738 --> 36:59.947
‎They're the problem.

597
37:00.448 --> 37:01.615
‎I'll ask again.

598
37:02.491 --> 37:04.368
‎Are there any attendings here

599
37:05.202 --> 37:07.580
‎willing to scrub in as lead surgeons?

600
37:27.308 --> 37:30.227
‎CASE 1: LEE HYEON-A, F/8

601
38:03.594 --> 38:05.012
‎Please.

602
38:38.796 --> 38:40.089
‎I can't believe all of you.

603
38:41.215 --> 38:44.260
‎However hopeless it may seem, ‎backing down like this is disgraceful.

604
38:44.760 --> 38:46.387
‎If you don't have the confidence,

605
38:46.470 --> 38:49.432
‎at least support the person ‎who has the courage to step up.

606
38:50.057 --> 38:51.600
‎Strike rally? IRB?

607
38:51.684 --> 38:53.269
‎That's all an excuse.

608
38:53.978 --> 38:55.729
‎I'm going to remember every person

609
38:56.355 --> 38:58.315
‎who walks out that door.

610
38:58.983 --> 39:00.776
‎You should all be ashamed.

611
39:08.200 --> 39:10.911
‎I can't believe nobody stepped up.

612
39:12.329 --> 39:14.039
‎She even groveled.

613
39:14.123 --> 39:15.708
‎I didn't grovel.

614
39:15.791 --> 39:16.959
‎I just bowed.

615
39:25.301 --> 39:26.469
‎I'm upset, but this is good.

616
39:29.597 --> 39:30.973
‎You know what, Dr. Gye?

617
39:31.849 --> 39:33.434
‎I still think you're amazing.

618
39:33.517 --> 39:34.977
‎You were incredible.

619
39:35.478 --> 39:38.105
‎Yeah. I agree with him.

620
39:39.565 --> 39:42.067
‎Dr. Gye, you were pretty cool.

621
39:44.111 --> 39:45.362
‎You too, Dr. Jo.

622
39:45.988 --> 39:48.491
‎You saw everyone leaving and said,

623
39:48.574 --> 39:50.034
‎"You should all be ashamed!"

624
39:52.453 --> 39:53.996
‎But do they even feel ashamed?

625
39:55.080 --> 39:56.248
‎What do you think?

626
39:56.332 --> 39:59.919
‎Is waiting for the IRB approval ‎really our only option?

627
40:01.378 --> 40:03.506
‎They say people die ‎when they act out of character.

628
40:04.006 --> 40:05.090
‎Are you dead?

629
40:05.925 --> 40:07.134
‎I'm just thinking.

630
40:07.801 --> 40:08.928
‎About what?

631
40:09.637 --> 40:10.763
‎Solo surgery.

632
40:10.846 --> 40:12.848
‎SOLO SURGERY: PRIMARY SURGEON ‎OPERATING WITHOUT AN ASSISTANT

633
40:22.525 --> 40:24.860
‎Nobody will come even if the IRB approves.

634
40:25.402 --> 40:27.780
‎That's not true. Count me in.

635
40:27.863 --> 40:28.864
‎But…

636
40:28.948 --> 40:30.783
‎I won't be much help, will I?

637
40:30.866 --> 40:31.700
‎Let's do it.

638
40:33.244 --> 40:34.119
‎Dr. Jo…

639
40:37.289 --> 40:39.959
‎Come on. I'll open the OR for you.

640
40:40.543 --> 40:42.419
‎Surgery isn't viable, ‎and approval won't change that.

641
40:42.503 --> 40:44.129
‎But we can't just sit and do nothing.

642
40:45.005 --> 40:48.634
‎I'll prep whatever materials you need ‎and help you practice operating solo.

643
40:49.134 --> 40:50.719
‎Let's make sure we do this right.

644
40:51.345 --> 40:53.597
‎All surgeries have been canceled anyway,

645
40:53.681 --> 40:54.765
‎so I have nothing to do.

646
40:57.851 --> 40:59.603
‎You never fail, right?

647
41:00.729 --> 41:03.232
‎Well, I never give up.

648
41:06.068 --> 41:07.194
‎Get up already.

649
41:08.529 --> 41:10.281
‎Let's go. There's no time.

650
41:10.364 --> 41:11.490
‎Get up, Dr. Gye.

651
41:20.624 --> 41:21.458
‎I got this.

652
41:23.961 --> 41:24.795
‎You got this.

653
41:42.104 --> 41:42.938
‎Stop right there.

654
41:44.607 --> 41:47.568
‎If you do that surgery, ‎I'm really going to fire you.

655
42:02.708 --> 42:04.209
‎Hey, answer me!

656
42:08.213 --> 42:09.757
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

657
42:10.341 --> 42:11.508
‎Clamping the IVC.

658
42:13.552 --> 42:14.803
‎Clamping the celiac trunk.

659
42:18.223 --> 42:21.018
‎Connecting the HTK. Starting perfusion.

660
42:24.104 --> 42:25.689
‎Beginning reconstruction.

661
42:28.192 --> 42:29.568
‎Mobilize the liver first.

662
42:31.236 --> 42:33.489
‎-Dissect the vessels-- ‎-Again.

663
42:34.865 --> 42:36.408
‎You need to shave off 30 minutes.

664
42:38.535 --> 42:39.912
‎There's just not enough time.

665
42:41.330 --> 42:43.165
‎I can't get the time down…

666
42:45.209 --> 42:46.710
‎They don't need to be a lead surgeon,

667
42:46.794 --> 42:48.879
‎but you need someone skilled to assist.

668
42:52.299 --> 42:53.342
‎Let's go again.

669
42:57.888 --> 42:59.598
‎Wow, this place is huge.

670
43:00.391 --> 43:03.602
‎Mom, it's even bigger than ‎when I saw it from up there.

671
43:05.688 --> 43:07.564
‎Hello, Dr. Gye.

672
43:07.648 --> 43:08.565
‎Hey.

673
43:09.775 --> 43:11.402
‎I thought looking around here first

674
43:11.485 --> 43:13.487
‎would help you feel less scared, Hyeon-a.

675
43:13.570 --> 43:14.405
‎How do you feel?

676
43:14.488 --> 43:16.323
‎I'm not scared at all.

677
43:16.824 --> 43:20.035
‎I already watched her operate on Snuggles.

678
43:20.619 --> 43:21.829
‎That's right.

679
43:22.913 --> 43:24.998
‎You'll lie down over there and sleep.

680
43:25.082 --> 43:27.876
‎By the time you wake up, it'll be over.

681
43:38.554 --> 43:40.055
‎Dr. Gye.

682
43:41.014 --> 43:41.932
‎Yeah?

683
43:42.015 --> 43:44.393
‎You operated on Ga-eul.

684
43:45.144 --> 43:46.520
‎Thank you.

685
43:47.521 --> 43:49.940
‎You operated on Snuggles too.

686
43:50.524 --> 43:51.692
‎Thank you.

687
43:52.693 --> 43:54.111
‎And…

688
43:55.112 --> 43:57.114
‎you agreed to operate on me

689
43:57.656 --> 43:59.700
‎when everyone else said no.

690
44:00.743 --> 44:02.286
‎Thank you.

691
44:06.248 --> 44:08.667
‎She's been wanting to thank you.

692
44:08.751 --> 44:10.836
‎You could've done that after the surgery.

693
44:11.962 --> 44:13.797
‎But I might not wake up.

694
44:32.024 --> 44:33.984
‎That won't happen, Hyeon-a.

695
44:35.402 --> 44:37.613
‎I don't ever…

696
44:39.156 --> 44:40.616
‎fail.

697
44:48.499 --> 44:50.167
‎I don't ever fail.

698
44:51.084 --> 44:52.753
‎I don't ever fail.

699
44:53.796 --> 44:55.464
‎I don't ever fail.

700
44:56.548 --> 44:59.176
‎I don't ever…

701
45:00.093 --> 45:01.512
‎fail.

702
45:07.768 --> 45:09.478
‎No more late-night snacks.

703
45:09.978 --> 45:11.730
‎Her surgery starts ‎the moment it's approved.

704
45:12.773 --> 45:15.234
‎She needs to fast ‎since we don't know when that'll be.

705
45:17.486 --> 45:18.654
‎Don't cry.

706
45:18.737 --> 45:21.657
‎You're her dad. ‎She's not crying, so you can't either.

707
45:21.740 --> 45:22.908
‎We can't cry.

708
45:24.159 --> 45:26.995
‎How's your injury ‎from the construction site?

709
45:28.413 --> 45:29.790
‎Go to the hospital.

710
45:29.873 --> 45:31.625
‎We still have some money left.

711
45:32.209 --> 45:33.877
‎Don't take on more work, okay?

712
45:36.046 --> 45:37.506
‎Let's do a video call tomorrow.

713
45:38.048 --> 45:39.466
‎I know you want to see Hyeon-a.

714
45:46.557 --> 45:47.766
‎She's not dead.

715
45:48.767 --> 45:49.851
‎Stop crying.

716
45:51.186 --> 45:52.396
‎I said stop crying.

717
45:53.313 --> 45:55.315
‎Stop crying, you dummy!

718
46:04.533 --> 46:06.201
‎So? What did they say?

719
46:07.494 --> 46:08.787
‎They said it's hard

720
46:08.870 --> 46:10.706
‎to schedule an IRB meeting ‎due to the strike.

721
46:10.789 --> 46:12.583
‎How does this relate to the strike?

722
46:12.666 --> 46:15.460
‎They need to account for hospital staffing ‎based on tomorrow's vote…

723
46:15.544 --> 46:16.545
‎I'll look into it.

724
46:16.628 --> 46:18.672
‎-But Dr. Jo-- ‎-Those jerks.

725
46:31.643 --> 46:33.353
‎Here. And Dr. Gye.

726
46:34.104 --> 46:36.940
‎Just focus on eating, ‎or you'll get indigestion.

727
46:37.524 --> 46:40.193
‎If your mind wanders, ‎you'll bite your tongue by accident.

728
46:48.660 --> 46:49.828
‎You're only just getting off?

729
46:49.911 --> 46:51.747
‎Everyone is working hard, so…

730
46:53.248 --> 46:54.666
‎What about you, Dr. Do?

731
46:54.750 --> 46:56.627
‎I need to stop by home

732
46:56.710 --> 46:58.545
‎and grab a few things.

733
47:00.088 --> 47:00.964
‎Dr. Do.

734
47:03.425 --> 47:04.843
‎Will you buy me a drink?

735
47:06.136 --> 47:07.095
‎What?

736
47:33.747 --> 47:36.333
‎I didn't bring you here because I'm broke.

737
47:36.833 --> 47:38.752
‎It's the only place ‎that sells non-alcoholic beer.

738
47:38.835 --> 47:40.420
‎Regular beer would've been fine.

739
47:41.171 --> 47:42.172
‎Or soju too.

740
47:42.255 --> 47:45.050
‎Don't say that, sir. No more drinking.

741
47:45.133 --> 47:46.593
‎Your wife will have my head.

742
47:48.762 --> 47:49.846
‎Have this instead.

743
47:52.307 --> 47:55.435
‎Any particular snack you'd like with this?

744
47:56.687 --> 47:58.438
‎You really like snacks, don't you?

745
48:00.190 --> 48:03.276
‎I still like snacks at this age.

746
48:18.709 --> 48:21.503
‎About the strike rally ‎in the conference hall…

747
48:22.212 --> 48:24.089
‎I heard Magnolia will be there too.

748
48:25.257 --> 48:29.219
‎Let's try to talk them out ‎of closing the hospital.

749
48:40.021 --> 48:41.857
‎I thought it'd feel good.

750
48:44.526 --> 48:47.112
‎I thought it'd feel good to see…

751
48:48.947 --> 48:51.074
‎Dr. Gye humble herself.

752
48:56.413 --> 48:58.039
‎I really did.

753
49:07.090 --> 49:09.718
‎This snack doesn't taste good anymore…

754
49:11.470 --> 49:12.679
‎even though it's my favorite.

755
49:29.738 --> 49:30.739
‎Stop right there.

756
49:37.329 --> 49:40.999
‎If you push through ‎an unapproved surgery and it fails,

757
49:41.082 --> 49:42.834
‎you'll take the fall for it.

758
49:43.418 --> 49:44.377
‎Oh, wait.

759
49:45.003 --> 49:47.506
‎Dr. Jo and the young doctor ‎will go down with you.

760
49:52.636 --> 49:54.679
‎What if they file a lawsuit later?

761
49:54.763 --> 49:56.181
‎What about our agency?

762
50:00.727 --> 50:02.854
‎Don't worry about us. We're fine.

763
50:03.855 --> 50:05.190
‎Cut it out, you two!

764
50:11.988 --> 50:14.199
‎I'm going to the hospital tomorrow ‎to end your contract.

765
50:15.742 --> 50:16.576
‎Aunt.

766
50:27.587 --> 50:29.005
‎It's her first doll.

767
50:31.007 --> 50:32.676
‎But it could also be her last.

768
50:49.985 --> 50:51.194
‎-Mom. ‎-Yes?

769
50:51.278 --> 50:52.988
‎I can't sleep because I'm hungry.

770
50:53.989 --> 50:55.532
‎Me too.

771
50:56.116 --> 50:57.701
‎But you can eat, Mom.

772
50:58.285 --> 50:59.369
‎No way.

773
51:02.205 --> 51:04.207
‎Should we just eat something?

774
51:04.708 --> 51:06.501
‎They might not even operate tomorrow.

775
51:06.585 --> 51:07.544
‎No.

776
51:08.128 --> 51:10.338
‎The doctor is working really hard.

777
51:11.006 --> 51:12.424
‎I can handle…

778
51:15.677 --> 51:16.636
‎Gummy candy.

779
51:18.680 --> 51:19.806
‎No, I need to tough it out.

780
51:21.725 --> 51:23.602
‎Okay. Let's tough it out together.

781
51:26.187 --> 51:27.147
‎-Mom. ‎-Yes?

782
51:27.230 --> 51:28.690
‎Then how about

783
51:28.773 --> 51:31.359
‎we play a game ‎and list the food we want to eat?

784
51:31.443 --> 51:32.319
‎Sounds good.

785
51:39.326 --> 51:40.327
‎Tangsuyuk.

786
51:41.411 --> 51:42.913
‎I want to eat that too.

787
51:42.996 --> 51:44.706
‎No, say something different.

788
51:47.167 --> 51:48.001
‎I think I lost.

789
51:48.084 --> 51:50.337
‎Yes, I won!

790
51:51.421 --> 51:52.714
‎You win again, Hyeon-a.

791
52:06.186 --> 52:07.103
‎Hyeon-a.

792
52:08.355 --> 52:09.314
‎Are you okay?

793
52:10.065 --> 52:10.941
‎You'll be fine.

794
52:11.775 --> 52:12.692
‎Mom…

795
52:14.861 --> 52:15.695
‎Mom…

796
52:16.404 --> 52:17.530
‎You're crying.

797
52:29.793 --> 52:32.253
‎DIRECTOR JANG'S LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

798
52:32.337 --> 52:35.507
‎LETTER OF RESIGNATION ‎GYE SU-JEONG

799
52:38.969 --> 52:41.304
‎Multivisceral ex vivo tumor resection ‎and autotransplantation.

800
52:41.388 --> 52:42.639
‎Let's begin.

801
52:42.722 --> 52:44.349
‎The goal is 15 hours.

802
52:45.266 --> 52:46.101
‎Let's hurry.

803
52:52.732 --> 52:54.150
‎OPERATION TIME

804
52:54.234 --> 52:56.027
‎TIME

805
52:56.111 --> 52:58.613
‎MAGNOLIA BREAKFAST MEETING

806
52:59.948 --> 53:00.865
‎What is it?

807
53:02.617 --> 53:03.493
‎What?

808
53:04.411 --> 53:07.247
‎How? The IRB hasn't approved it.

809
53:07.330 --> 53:10.542
‎The kid had an emergency overnight, ‎so she went ahead with it.

810
53:11.501 --> 53:14.504
‎Dr. Jo kept the OR open, just in case.

811
53:15.714 --> 53:17.215
‎In emergency cases,

812
53:17.298 --> 53:20.218
‎hospital rules allow us to operate first

813
53:20.301 --> 53:23.847
‎and submit a report later ‎if surgery is the only option--

814
53:23.930 --> 53:25.306
‎Who's there?

815
53:26.224 --> 53:28.727
‎Just two, ‎Dr. Jo Won-jin and Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

816
53:30.270 --> 53:35.275
‎Is she really going to ‎perform that surgery alone?

817
53:43.199 --> 53:45.535
‎This whole thing is a mass?

818
53:45.618 --> 53:47.704
‎MASS: AN ABNORMAL LUMP IN THE BODY

819
54:02.010 --> 54:04.387
‎We'll now hear opening remarks

820
54:04.471 --> 54:06.806
‎from President Kim Chang-su ‎of the Seonam Medical Association.

821
54:14.314 --> 54:16.441
‎VOTE ON NATIONWIDE INTERN RESIDENT STRIKE

822
54:19.652 --> 54:22.864
‎Taking their white coats ‎off and on like this can't be easy.

823
54:23.823 --> 54:24.783
‎We're here today

824
54:25.575 --> 54:30.288
‎to lay the groundwork for a fight ‎where our white coats are on the line.

825
54:33.458 --> 54:34.542
‎How much longer?

826
54:35.126 --> 54:36.419
‎I'm almost done.

827
54:36.503 --> 54:37.921
‎Just need to clamp one more vessel.

828
54:42.008 --> 54:42.842
‎12:00 P.M. ‎SUNDAY, MAY 3

829
54:42.926 --> 54:44.677
‎Holding a vote today

830
54:44.761 --> 54:48.640
‎proves that our approach ‎follows a more democratic process…

831
54:48.723 --> 54:52.102
‎She's probably ages away ‎from clamping the IVC, right?

832
54:53.353 --> 54:55.772
‎Who knows? It's Gye Su-jeong, after all.

833
54:58.399 --> 54:59.275
‎Right.

834
54:59.818 --> 55:01.528
‎Clamping the IVC. Vascular clamp.

835
55:01.611 --> 55:04.197
‎VASCULAR CLAMP: ‎USED TO TEMPORARILY BLOCK BLOOD FLOW

836
55:04.280 --> 55:06.157
‎-Heparin-- ‎-5,000 units in.

837
55:06.241 --> 55:07.492
‎HEPARIN: AN ANTICOAGULANT

838
55:10.495 --> 55:12.789
‎We will now vote on the motion

839
55:12.872 --> 55:14.833
‎to submit our resignations.

840
55:15.667 --> 55:17.335
‎Before we begin,

841
55:17.418 --> 55:20.338
‎there will be a short briefing ‎on the requests made by

842
55:20.421 --> 55:22.173
‎the Korean Intern Resident Association.

843
55:22.257 --> 55:23.883
‎Cardiothoracic surgery resident,

844
55:23.967 --> 55:27.095
‎-Dr. Lee Mal-geum, will now… ‎-She can get to that phase on her own.

845
55:27.178 --> 55:28.721
‎Gye Su-jeong can, for sure.

846
55:30.181 --> 55:32.058
‎Even if she has clamped the IVC,

847
55:32.851 --> 55:34.561
‎the real surgery starts now.

848
55:37.147 --> 55:38.106
‎Right.

849
55:38.731 --> 55:39.566
‎Hello.

850
55:39.649 --> 55:42.402
‎I'm Lee Mal-geum, a third-year ‎cardiothoracic surgery resident.

851
55:44.070 --> 55:45.405
‎Let's open the shunt.

852
55:45.488 --> 55:48.533
‎SHUNT: A PASSAGE THAT REDIRECTS ‎THE FLOW OF BLOOD OR BODILY FLUIDS

853
55:49.075 --> 55:50.160
‎Focus.

854
55:51.452 --> 55:52.328
‎Right.

855
56:06.259 --> 56:10.138
‎This has never been just about numbers.

856
56:11.264 --> 56:13.141
‎We have warned that frontline healthcare

857
56:13.224 --> 56:15.226
‎has already reached a breaking point.

858
56:16.561 --> 56:19.898
‎But the government views this crisis ‎as nothing more than…

859
56:28.740 --> 56:31.201
‎What was that? Isn't that Dr. Do Yun-sik?

860
56:32.285 --> 56:33.661
‎What are you doing, Dr. Do?

861
56:33.745 --> 56:35.121
‎-What? ‎-Going to the restroom?

862
56:35.205 --> 56:36.497
‎No, sir.

863
56:36.581 --> 56:39.083
‎-Damn it. ‎-Dr. Do, don't tell me…

864
56:40.793 --> 56:44.339
‎Dr. Bae, look after the director for me.

865
56:44.923 --> 56:46.007
‎-Director Bu. ‎-Dr. Do!

866
56:46.090 --> 56:47.008
‎Yes?

867
56:48.968 --> 56:49.969
‎I…

868
56:52.847 --> 56:53.932
‎Oh, screw it.

869
57:01.981 --> 57:03.441
‎-Are you all right? ‎-Damn it.

870
57:12.242 --> 57:13.117
‎Goodness.

871
57:23.002 --> 57:25.588
‎That punk… Which way is it?

872
57:26.631 --> 57:27.799
‎We prayed so hard

873
57:27.882 --> 57:30.176
‎for that beat-up car to break down safely.

874
57:30.260 --> 57:31.344
‎Looks like it worked.

875
57:31.427 --> 57:32.804
‎Why won't she answer?

876
57:32.887 --> 57:35.974
‎But why did it have to break down ‎at a time like this?

877
57:36.724 --> 57:39.352
‎I'm going to kill that punk.

878
57:43.648 --> 57:46.359
‎First, reflect on on-site feedback…

879
57:46.442 --> 57:47.527
‎Where did Dr. Do go?

880
57:49.112 --> 57:50.154
‎I'm not sure, sir.

881
57:50.238 --> 57:52.991
‎As this issue will shape the future ‎of Korean healthcare,

882
57:53.074 --> 57:56.911
‎we need proper discussions with experts ‎and organizations on the frontline.

883
57:57.787 --> 58:00.164
‎If the government wants the best ‎for Korean healthcare,

884
58:00.248 --> 58:02.375
‎they must listen ‎to frontline professionals.

885
58:02.875 --> 58:04.460
‎We need meaningful discussion…

886
58:09.257 --> 58:11.676
‎Dr. Do Yun-sik, general surgery.

887
58:11.759 --> 58:12.885
‎Dr. Do.

888
58:12.969 --> 58:14.053
‎Let's do a time-out…

889
58:14.137 --> 58:15.597
‎Just get in here and help.

890
58:15.680 --> 58:16.556
‎Right.

891
58:16.639 --> 58:19.058
‎Prepare… prepare the shunt…

892
58:19.767 --> 58:21.936
‎-You did it already? ‎-Breathe, Dr. Do.

893
58:22.020 --> 58:23.396
‎Your hands are shaking.

894
58:23.479 --> 58:26.441
‎Wait. Are you the only one assisting?

895
58:26.524 --> 58:27.900
‎This is insane!

896
58:29.152 --> 58:31.821
‎Still, you're two steps ahead ‎of what I expected.

897
58:31.904 --> 58:34.365
‎I'm a step behind where I want to be.

898
58:34.449 --> 58:35.450
‎Yeah.

899
58:35.533 --> 58:37.035
‎Kind of like my career after today.

900
58:38.202 --> 58:39.370
‎Satinsky clamp.

901
58:40.455 --> 58:41.831
‎Clamping the celiac trunk.

902
58:41.914 --> 58:44.000
‎SATINSKY CLAMP: USED TO RESTRICT ‎BLOOD FLOW OF A MAJOR VESSEL

903
58:50.757 --> 58:52.508
‎Why is the damn elevator so slow?

904
59:05.772 --> 59:06.773
‎Seriously?

905
59:09.275 --> 59:10.193
‎Alcohol?

906
59:11.402 --> 59:12.278
‎Are you crazy?

907
59:12.362 --> 59:14.322
‎You saw her resignation letter, ‎went back inside,

908
59:14.405 --> 59:15.490
‎and grabbed this?

909
59:15.573 --> 59:16.824
‎What was I supposed to do?

910
59:17.325 --> 59:18.159
‎Tell me.

911
59:18.242 --> 59:20.995
‎But you worked so hard to get sober.

912
59:21.579 --> 59:22.580
‎Did you drink any?

913
59:23.081 --> 59:24.916
‎No, not yet.

914
59:24.999 --> 59:26.167
‎Give me your hand.

915
59:26.668 --> 59:27.710
‎Now.

916
59:33.174 --> 59:34.509
‎You know this won't last long.

917
59:36.594 --> 59:38.096
‎And you know we can't do this often.

918
59:41.933 --> 59:43.726
‎All right. Let's go.

919
59:44.227 --> 59:47.188
‎Su-jeong, you punk. ‎Your aunt will chew you out.

920
01:00:12.130 --> 01:00:13.256
‎Dissection complete.

921
01:00:13.881 --> 01:00:16.175
‎Time to take them out.

922
01:00:57.759 --> 01:01:00.928
‎We urge the government once again ‎to present a reasonable alternative.

923
01:01:01.471 --> 01:01:02.430
‎Thank you.

924
01:01:07.852 --> 01:01:09.228
‎1:08 P.M. ‎SUNDAY, MAY 3

925
01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:17.403
‎Dr. Ma.

926
01:01:18.279 --> 01:01:19.363
‎Yes, sir.

927
01:01:19.447 --> 01:01:20.740
‎Aren't you going to continue?

928
01:01:20.823 --> 01:01:22.074
‎Right, sir.

929
01:01:27.789 --> 01:01:30.458
‎Thank you for the briefing, Dr. Lee.

930
01:01:31.042 --> 01:01:33.169
‎We will now begin the vote.

931
01:01:33.669 --> 01:01:35.254
‎The vote to submit resignations

932
01:01:35.338 --> 01:01:38.257
‎needs to clear an 80% majority.

933
01:01:49.393 --> 01:01:50.228
‎Connecting the HTK.

934
01:01:51.187 --> 01:01:52.271
‎Starting perfusion.

935
01:01:52.355 --> 01:01:54.607
‎PERFUSION: PASSING FLUID ‎THROUGH VESSELS OF AN ORGAN OR TISSUE

936
01:02:01.572 --> 01:02:03.783
‎Now the real work begins.

937
01:02:03.866 --> 01:02:04.700
‎Are we…

938
01:02:05.660 --> 01:02:07.328
‎Are we really doing this? Just us?

939
01:02:07.411 --> 01:02:08.663
‎Yes.

940
01:02:09.539 --> 01:02:10.748
‎I'm going to lose it.

941
01:02:10.832 --> 01:02:13.417
‎BP is 50 over 30. If it drops lower…

942
01:02:13.501 --> 01:02:14.710
‎It'll cause brain damage.

943
01:02:14.794 --> 01:02:15.878
‎I know that, you punk.

944
01:02:16.379 --> 01:02:18.631
‎Go and page someone.

945
01:02:18.714 --> 01:02:22.635
‎Page anyone who can assist. ‎We can't do this by ourselves.

946
01:02:22.718 --> 01:02:25.972
‎Just get someone in here!

947
01:02:49.704 --> 01:02:51.664
‎Dr. Jang Hui-suk, a surgeon.

948
01:02:54.584 --> 01:02:55.501
‎What?

949
01:02:56.335 --> 01:02:57.670
‎Who?

950
01:02:57.753 --> 01:02:59.463
‎Who… who are you?

951
01:02:59.547 --> 01:03:00.882
‎Jang Hui-suk?

952
01:03:00.965 --> 01:03:02.008
‎Ms. Jang?

953
01:03:02.884 --> 01:03:03.968
‎Harmonic, please.

954
01:03:04.051 --> 01:03:06.429
‎What did you say? Ms. Jang?

955
01:03:06.512 --> 01:03:08.890
‎What? Who are you again?

956
01:03:09.765 --> 01:03:10.641
‎She's…

957
01:03:11.183 --> 01:03:12.393
‎my mentor.

958
01:03:27.825 --> 01:03:30.786
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

959
01:04:09.909 --> 01:04:12.870
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

960
01:04:12.954 --> 01:04:14.997
‎I'm going to make sure

961
01:04:15.081 --> 01:04:17.083
‎Hyeon-a gets to grow up.

962
01:04:17.166 --> 01:04:18.793
‎If we are doctors,

963
01:04:18.876 --> 01:04:20.920
‎where should we be right now?

964
01:04:21.671 --> 01:04:23.172
‎Stop the surgery!

965
01:04:23.255 --> 01:04:26.050
‎We're seeing this surgery ‎through to the end.

966
01:04:26.133 --> 01:04:28.177
‎You disregarded it ‎to proceed with the surgery

967
01:04:28.260 --> 01:04:29.512
‎and put the patient in danger.

968
01:04:29.595 --> 01:04:32.139
‎The hospital is short-staffed ‎because of the strike.

969
01:04:32.223 --> 01:04:35.267
‎I don't regret taking part in the surgery.

970
01:04:35.351 --> 01:04:36.435
‎Gye Su-jeong.

971
01:04:37.019 --> 01:04:38.771
‎Contract termination remains in effect.

972
01:04:38.854 --> 01:04:43.859
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
